   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing as a cyclic peptide, but the stereochemistry is partly assumed rather than read from the wedges. I traced the residues from the C-terminal glycinamide back towards the N-terminus.\n\n**Residues, in order from the C-terminus:**\n- Gly-NH2\n- Cys, whose side-chain sulfur carries CH2C(=O)\u2013 and closes onto the nitrogen of Tyr\n- Leu\n- N-methyl-norleucine\n- N-methyl-norleucine\n- Trp whose indole nitrogen carries CH2COOH\n- a diamino acid with a two-carbon side chain (\u03b1-carbon, CH2, CH2, NH), which I read as Dab\n- Trp\n- 4-hydroxyproline\n- Val\n- Dap (2,3-diaminopropionic acid)\n- Pro\n- Asn\n- N-methyl-Ala\n- Tyr\n\n**Side-chain bridge:** the Dab side-chain NH and the Dap side-chain NH are joined by \u2013CH2\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH2\u2013.\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- I assigned L-configuration to the standard residues by assumption.\n- The N-methyl-Ala and 4-hydroxyproline stereocentres, and the Cys configuration, were not resolved from the image. I guessed those, so they may be wrong.\n- The two carbinol carbons in the linker are drawn with plain bonds, so they carry no stereo.\n\nI checked the ring-closure labels by hand but did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CSCC%10=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCC)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCC)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1cn(CC(=O)O)c2ccccc12)NC(=O)[C@H](CCNCC(O)COCC(O)CN%12)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)NC(=O)[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)CN1C(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](C%12)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H](C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)N%10"
